{"id":"u-f2a2f463-4ce9-4347-b0c5-ab10bdfb32dd","src":"community","title":"⛈️Biffed It!⛈️","author":"Thunder Peeler","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/5HSw4f-explosivo-1","desc":"Three days, one for push, pull, and leg movements. This is all about progressive overload. \n\nThe primary reason I added overlapping exercises into the next day is because I want to form an annular cycle. Simple explanation; working a muscle group 1 day a week is good, 2 days a week shows significant growth, and then any day after in a week usually has a shallow exponential growth. If this schedule only has 3 days, I want to provide maximized results.\n\nStart in the lower rep ranges (for example, if the rep range is 10-14, start at 10 reps). Then each week after, lift 1 extra rep per set to reach the end. After 4 weeks, add 5 lbs for upper body exercises & 10 lbs for lower body exercises (if you can). Repeat the rep ranges for the next cycle of 5 weeks, then repeat. Add 5 lbs for upper body & 10 lbs for the lower body after the 5 weeks are renewed.\n\nThe reason this is set at 5 weeks is because as you are doing full body workouts at a lower RPE, you will have great muscle recovery. You want to work towards failure but you will have much more reps in reserve in the beginning of this.\n\nI set this workout for 2 (maybe even 2 ½ hours) hours given I add cardio but I don't track it via Boostcamp.","level":["Advanced"],"goals":["Athletics","Bodyweight Fitness","Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":120,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-27T00:18:24.850Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Push (With Pull Overlap)","Pull (With Legs Overlap)","Legs (With Push Overlap)"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Seated Dip (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":14,"rpe":8,"x":8}]},{"n":"Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":14,"rpe":8,"x":8}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":14,"rpe":8,"x":8}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":14,"rpe":8,"x":8}]